      "summary": "ស្វែងយល់ពីកម្មវិធី Real-time (Polling vs WebSockets)៖\n\n- **Short & Long Polling**៖ Client ត្រូវបើក HTTP Requests ថ្មីជាប្រចាំ បង្កើត Server Load និង Latency ខ្ពស់។\n- **WebSockets**៖ បង្កើត Full-Duplex Connection តែមួយ គ្មាន Header Overhead និងបញ្ជូនទិន្នន័យភ្លាមៗ (Instant Data)។\n- **Use Cases**៖ សមស្របសម្រាប់ Live Chat, Instant Notifications, Collaborative Editing, និង Real-time Dashboards។",
      "tip": "Don't use HTTP short-polling for real-time features! Polling every 2 seconds consumes massive bandwidth and wastes server CPU.",
      "objective": "Understand the differences between HTTP Polling, Server-Sent Events (SSE), and WebSockets.",
      "expectedOutcome": "Clear criteria for choosing between HTTP, SSE, and full-duplex WebSockets.",
      "codeSnippet": "// Comparison:\n// 1. Short Polling:   Client asks every 2s: \"New data? New data? New data?\" (High overhead)\n// 2. Long Polling:    Client asks; server holds connection open until data arrives (Moderate)\n// 3. SSE:             Unidirectional server-to-client streaming over HTTP (Great for tickers)\n// 4. WebSocket:       Bi-directional, persistent TCP connection with sub-millisecond frames (Ideal for chat/gaming)"
